IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ntmaccc-dates`

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT) -- the questions of a person with a claim on the Commission.
--
-- SEAT: the person claiming under the MAC scheme (the no-fault scheme of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979):
-- usually the person injured in a motor accident, or a dependant after a death, and also a former customer of the
-- Territory Insurance Office whose policy or deposit stayed with the Commission. "Is the company handling my claim
-- acting for the Commission?", "Whom can I hold liable?", "Does the Territory stand behind what I am owed?", "Can my
-- benefits be paid out of the Fund?", "Is my public hospital treatment reimbursed from the Fund?", "Was it an offence to
-- disclose information about me?", "Does what I did with TIO still count?", "Who deals with my old TIO policy or
-- deposit?". The Commission, the Commissioner, the Minister and the Treasurer get no seat: what they decide or are
-- satisfied of is asked as a fact.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a date, a number, a choice from a list). No question takes a DEONTIC or an
-- EVENT. The one rule the Act lays on others for the claimant's protection (the s 28 prohibition on disclosing
-- information obtained in administering the Act) is a regulative rule (SHANT) run inside a question.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (definitions: MAC business, MAC scheme, Fund), s 5 (the Commission continues TIO; may sue and
-- be sued; how constituted), s 7(a) and s 8 (administering the MAC scheme), s 9 (delegation, including to a
-- non-government delegate by delegation contract, and sub-delegation), s 11 (business names), s 12(3) (documents under
-- seal), s 15 (protection from liability), s 16 (the Fund is the Territory's, not a trust), s 17(2) (what the Fund may
-- pay for), s 18 (reimbursing the Territory for public health services to MAC claimants), s 27 (the Territory's
-- guarantee), s 28 (confidentiality offence), s 30 (residual insurance business), ss 31, 33, 34 (residual banking
-- business), s 43 (continuation of ongoing matters). Out: the Commission's constitution and management (ss 6, 10, 13, 14,
-- 19-25, 29, 36, 37, 41, 42), s 4, s 26 (borrowed Government Owned Corporations Act sections, not deposited), s 32, s 38,
-- s 39 (spent or not reaching a claimant), s 1, s 2: machinery. Reasons in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT), Act No. 42 of 2014, reprint REPM059 as in force at
-- 1 July 2021, retrieved 6 November 2026, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/Motor-Accidents-Compensation-Commission-Act-2014-NT-current-reprint-REPM059.txt. No
-- regulation sets a number this encoding needs; the value of a penalty unit (Penalty Units Act 2009, not deposited) is
-- asked.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; quoted under the NT
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). This is not an official version of the Act.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Judgments the Act hands to someone else are INPUTS. Answers follow
-- the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (NOTES.md): an answer that is the text's own no is marked "(the
-- text's no)"; an answer where the text does not answer is marked "NOTHING-kind".

§ `Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT): the questions of a person with a claim on the Commission`

§§ `s 5, s 9, s 11 -- Who is dealing with my claim`

-- s 5(1): the Territory Insurance Office "continues as the same corporate entity under the name of the Motor Accidents
-- (Compensation) Commission". s 5(3)(a): the Commission is constituted by the Commissioner and any Associate
-- Commissioners. s 7(a): its function is "to administer the MAC scheme in accordance with the Motor Accidents
-- (Compensation) Act 1979"; s 8: it has "all the powers of an individual". s 11: it "may use and operate under one or
-- more business or trading names approved by the Minister". s 9(1): it may delegate its powers and functions to (a) the
-- Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner, (b) a Chief Executive Officer or a public sector employee, (c) a statutory
-- corporation, or (d) "with the approval of the Minister, any other person (a non-government delegate)". s 9(2): a
-- delegation under (1)(d) "must be made by written contract" (a delegation contract). s 9(3): the Commission "must not
-- enter into a delegation contract unless the terms of the contract have been approved by the Minister". s 9(4)(a): a
-- non-government delegate may sub-delegate "if doing so is permitted by the delegation contract". s 9(5): a contract
-- under s 9 of the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014 "is taken to be a contract under subsection (2) making a
-- delegation under subsection (1)(d)".
DECLARE `Who is handling my claim` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission, under its own name`
    `the Commission, under a business or trading name`
    `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner`
    `a Chief Executive Officer or a public sector employee`
    `a statutory corporation`
    `a private company or other non-government person`
    `someone to whom that private company or person passed the work on`

DECLARE `Is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commission administers the MAC scheme under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 7(a)), with all the powers of an individual (s 8); it is the Territory Insurance Office continued under a new name (s 5(1))`
    `yes: the Commission may operate under a business or trading name the Minister has approved (s 11)`
    `this Act does not say: s 11 lets the Commission use only names the Minister has approved, and says nothing of other names (NOTHING-kind)`
    `yes: the Commission is constituted by the Commissioner and any Associate Commissioners (s 5(3)(a)), and may delegate to them (s 9(1)(a))`
    `yes: the Commission may delegate its powers and functions to a Chief Executive Officer, a public sector employee or a statutory corporation (s 9(1)(b), (c)), and has done so`
    `this Act does not say: without a delegation from the Commission, s 9 gives them nothing (NOTHING-kind)`
    `yes: a non-government delegate under the contract made in the sale of TIO, which is taken to be a delegation contract (s 9(5))`
    `yes: a non-government delegate, with the Minister's approval and a written delegation contract whose terms the Minister approved (s 9(1)(d), (2), (3))`
    `no: a delegation to a non-government person needs the Minister's approval (s 9(1)(d), the text's no)`
    `no: a delegation to a non-government person must be made by written contract (s 9(2), the text's no)`
    `no: the Commission must not enter into a delegation contract unless the Minister has approved its terms (s 9(3), the text's no)`
    `yes: a sub-delegate of a non-government delegate, as the delegation contract permits (s 9(4)(a))`
    `no: a non-government delegate may sub-delegate only if the delegation contract permits it (s 9(4)(a), the text's no)`

-- The s 9(1)(d), (2), (3) and (5) test for a non-government delegate. s 9(5) settles it on its own; otherwise all three
-- conditions must hold. Fork F1: a missing approval or written contract is the text's no.
GIVEN `made in the sale of TIO` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister approved the delegation` IS A BOOLEAN, `written contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister approved the terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-government delegate under s 9` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms` IF
        `made in the sale of TIO`
    OR  (`Minister approved the delegation` AND `written contract` AND `Minister approved the terms`)

GIVEN `made in the sale of TIO` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister approved the delegation` IS A BOOLEAN, `written contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister approved the terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission`
`why a non-government person is not a delegate` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `made in the sale of TIO` THEN `yes: a non-government delegate under the contract made in the sale of TIO, which is taken to be a delegation contract (s 9(5))`
        IF (NOT `Minister approved the delegation`) THEN `no: a delegation to a non-government person needs the Minister's approval (s 9(1)(d), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `written contract`) THEN `no: a delegation to a non-government person must be made by written contract (s 9(2), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `Minister approved the terms`) THEN `no: the Commission must not enter into a delegation contract unless the Minister has approved its terms (s 9(3), the text's no)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: a non-government delegate, with the Minister's approval and a written delegation contract whose terms the Minister approved (s 9(1)(d), (2), (3))`

@export Is the body or person handling my motor accident claim acting for the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission of the Northern Territory (s 5, s 9, s 11)? The Commission may act under an approved business name or through delegates, including a private claims company under a delegation contract.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who is handling my claim` @desc Who is handling your claim under the MAC scheme: the Commission under its own name, the Commission under a business or trading name, the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner, a Chief Executive Officer or a public sector employee, a statutory corporation, a private company or other non-government person, or someone to whom that private company or person passed the work on
      `name approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the Commission is using a business or trading name: whether the Minister approved that name (otherwise any value; not used)
      `delegated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a Chief Executive Officer, public sector employee or statutory corporation is handling it: whether the Commission delegated the power or function to them (otherwise any value; not used)
      `made in the sale of TIO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a private company or person is involved: whether its contract with the Commission was made under section 9 of the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014
      `Minister approved the delegation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a private company or person is involved: whether the Minister approved the delegation to it
      `written contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a private company or person is involved: whether the delegation was made by a written contract between the Commission and it
      `Minister approved the terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a private company or person is involved: whether the Minister approved the terms of that contract
      `sub-delegation permitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone the private company passed the work on to is handling it: whether the delegation contract permits the company to sub-delegate
GIVETH A `Is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission`
`s 5, s 9, s 11 -- is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission` `who` `name approved` `delegated` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms` `sub-delegation permitted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the Commission, under its own name` THEN `yes: the Commission administers the MAC scheme under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 7(a)), with all the powers of an individual (s 8); it is the Territory Insurance Office continued under a new name (s 5(1))`
    WHEN `the Commission, under a business or trading name` THEN
        IF `name approved`
        THEN `yes: the Commission may operate under a business or trading name the Minister has approved (s 11)`
        ELSE `this Act does not say: s 11 lets the Commission use only names the Minister has approved, and says nothing of other names (NOTHING-kind)`
    WHEN `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner` THEN `yes: the Commission is constituted by the Commissioner and any Associate Commissioners (s 5(3)(a)), and may delegate to them (s 9(1)(a))`
    WHEN `a Chief Executive Officer or a public sector employee` THEN `public delegate` `delegated`
    WHEN `a statutory corporation` THEN `public delegate` `delegated`
    WHEN `a private company or other non-government person` THEN
        `why a non-government person is not a delegate` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms`
    WHEN `someone to whom that private company or person passed the work on` THEN
        IF `a non-government delegate under s 9` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms`
        THEN IF `sub-delegation permitted`
             THEN `yes: a sub-delegate of a non-government delegate, as the delegation contract permits (s 9(4)(a))`
             ELSE `no: a non-government delegate may sub-delegate only if the delegation contract permits it (s 9(4)(a), the text's no)`
        ELSE `why a non-government person is not a delegate` `made in the sale of TIO` `Minister approved the delegation` `written contract` `Minister approved the terms`
    WHERE
        `public delegate` `d` MEANS
            IF `d`
            THEN `yes: the Commission may delegate its powers and functions to a Chief Executive Officer, a public sector employee or a statutory corporation (s 9(1)(b), (c)), and has done so`
            ELSE `this Act does not say: without a delegation from the Commission, s 9 gives them nothing (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 5(2)(c), s 15 -- Whom I can hold liable`

-- s 5(2)(c): the Commission "may sue and be sued". s 15(1): "A person is not civilly or criminally liable for an act
-- done or omitted to be done by the person in good faith in the exercise of a power or performance of a function as the
-- Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner." s 15(2): "In addition, the person is not civilly or criminally liable for
-- an act done or omitted to be done by the Commission in the exercise of a power or performance of a function under this
-- Act." (no good-faith condition: finding 2). s 15(3): neither "affect[s] any liability the Territory or the Commission
-- would, apart from those subsections, have for the act or omission". s 15(4): "exercise" and "performance" include
-- the purported exercise and performance. Good faith is for a court: asked.
DECLARE `Whom I want to hold liable` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission`
    `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally`
    `the Northern Territory`

DECLARE `What was done or not done` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner's or Associate Commissioner's own act or omission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, a power or function as Commissioner`
    `an act or omission of the Commission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, its powers or functions, including administering the MAC scheme`
    `something the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner did outside those roles`

DECLARE `Can I hold them liable` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission may be sued (s 5(2)(c)); s 15 does not affect any liability the Commission has (s 15(3)); whether it is liable is for the general law and the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
    `s 15 does not affect any liability the Territory has (s 15(3)), and the Territory guarantees the Commission's liabilities in the MAC business (s 27); beyond that, this Act does not say (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
    `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission done in good faith in that role (s 15(1), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
    `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission of the Commission, whether or not in good faith (s 15(2), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
    `this Act does not protect them: the act was not in good faith, so s 15(1) does not apply; whether they are liable is for the general law (NOTHING-kind)`
    `this Act does not say: s 15 protects only acts in the role of Commissioner or Associate Commissioner, or of the Commission (NOTHING-kind)`

@export Can I hold the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission, the Commissioner personally, or the Northern Territory liable for what was done or not done about my claim (s 5(2)(c), s 15)?
GIVEN `whom` IS A `Whom I want to hold liable` @desc Whom you want to hold liable: the Commission, the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally, or the Northern Territory
      `what` IS A `What was done or not done` @desc What was done or not done: the Commissioner's own act or omission in that role (including a purported exercise of a power), an act or omission of the Commission (including in administering the MAC scheme), or something the Commissioner did outside those roles
      `good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or omission was done in good faith (a court decides this; answer as you would put it)
GIVETH A `Can I hold them liable`
`s 5(2)(c), s 15 -- can I hold them liable` `whom` `what` `good faith` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whom`
    WHEN `the Commission` THEN `the Commission may be sued (s 5(2)(c)); s 15 does not affect any liability the Commission has (s 15(3)); whether it is liable is for the general law and the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
    WHEN `the Northern Territory` THEN `s 15 does not affect any liability the Territory has (s 15(3)), and the Territory guarantees the Commission's liabilities in the MAC business (s 27); beyond that, this Act does not say (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
    WHEN `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` THEN
        CONSIDER `what`
        WHEN `the Commissioner's or Associate Commissioner's own act or omission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, a power or function as Commissioner` THEN
            IF `good faith`
            THEN `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission done in good faith in that role (s 15(1), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
            ELSE `this Act does not protect them: the act was not in good faith, so s 15(1) does not apply; whether they are liable is for the general law (NOTHING-kind)`
        WHEN `an act or omission of the Commission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, its powers or functions, including administering the MAC scheme` THEN `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission of the Commission, whether or not in good faith (s 15(2), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
        WHEN `something the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner did outside those roles` THEN `this Act does not say: s 15 protects only acts in the role of Commissioner or Associate Commissioner, or of the Commission (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 27 -- Whether the Territory stands behind what I am owed`

-- s 3: "MAC business means the part of the Commission's business that relates to administering the MAC scheme and
-- managing the Fund." s 27(1): "All liabilities of the Commission in relation to the MAC business are guaranteed by the
-- Territory." s 27(2): payable from the Central Holding Authority. The Commission's other business (the residual
-- insurance business, s 30; the residual banking business, ss 33, 34) lies outside the words of s 27: a scope limit
-- without "only", so NOTHING-kind (fork F3).
DECLARE `What the Commission owes me` IS ONE OF
    `benefits or another liability under the MAC scheme or out of the Fund`
    `a liability of TIO's insurance business that was not sold`
    `a deposit or other liability of TIO's banking business that was not sold`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Does the Territory guarantee it` IS ONE OF
    `yes: all liabilities of the Commission in relation to the MAC business are guaranteed by the Territory (s 27(1)), and amounts under the guarantee are paid from the Central Holding Authority (s 27(2))`
    `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business only, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind); for the residual banking business, the moneys held for it are the Territory's property (s 34(1))`
    `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind)`

@export If the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission owes me something, does the Northern Territory guarantee it (s 27)?
GIVEN `owed` IS A `What the Commission owes me` @desc What the Commission owes you: benefits or another liability under the MAC scheme or out of the Fund; a liability of TIO's insurance business that was not sold; a deposit or other liability of TIO's banking business that was not sold; or something else
GIVETH A `Does the Territory guarantee it`
`s 27 -- does the Territory guarantee what the Commission owes me` `owed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `owed`
    WHEN `benefits or another liability under the MAC scheme or out of the Fund` THEN `yes: all liabilities of the Commission in relation to the MAC business are guaranteed by the Territory (s 27(1)), and amounts under the guarantee are paid from the Central Holding Authority (s 27(2))`
    WHEN `a deposit or other liability of TIO's banking business that was not sold` THEN `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business only, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind); for the residual banking business, the moneys held for it are the Territory's property (s 34(1))`
    OTHERWISE `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 16, s 17 -- What the Fund may pay for`

-- s 16(2): the assets of the Fund are the property of the Territory, held by the Commission on its behalf; s 16(3): "a
-- trust is not created in relation to the Fund" and the Commission "is not a trustee". s 17(2): "The Commission may pay
-- amounts out of the Fund only for the following purposes: (a) payment of benefits under the Motor Accident
-- (Compensation) Act 1979 [sic: finding 4]; (b) administration of the MAC Scheme; (c) management of the Fund; (d)
-- payment of amounts payable by the Commission under a MAC management agreement; (e) discharge of any other liabilities
-- in relation to the MAC business; (f) payment of amounts required to be paid out of the Fund under section 14(3), 18,
-- 19 or 20; (g) promotion of road safety." A list closed with "only": outside it, the text's no.
DECLARE `What would be paid out of the Fund` IS ONE OF
    `benefits under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979`
    `the cost of administering the MAC scheme`
    `the cost of managing the Fund`
    `amounts the Commission owes under a contract delegating MAC work (a MAC management agreement)`
    `another liability in relation to the MAC business`
    `staff and facilities, reimbursing public health services, the prudential supervision fee, or a surplus paid to the Territory (s 14(3), 18, 19, 20)`
    `promoting road safety`
    `something else, such as a liability of TIO's former insurance or banking business`

DECLARE `Can it be paid out of the Fund` IS ONE OF
    `yes: that is one of the purposes for which the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund (s 17(2)); the Fund belongs to the Territory and is held by the Commission for it, not on trust (s 16(2), (3))`
    `no: the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund only for the purposes listed in s 17(2), and this is not one of them (the text's no)`

GIVEN `what` IS A `What would be paid out of the Fund`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a purpose listed in s 17(2)` `what` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `something else, such as a liability of TIO's former insurance or banking business` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Can this be paid out of the Northern Territory's Motor Accidents (Compensation) Fund -- for example my benefits under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 16, s 17(2))?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What would be paid out of the Fund` @desc What would be paid: benefits under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979; the cost of administering the MAC scheme; the cost of managing the Fund; amounts owed under a MAC management agreement; another liability in relation to the MAC business; staff and facilities, reimbursing public health services, the prudential supervision fee or a surplus paid to the Territory; promoting road safety; or something else, such as a liability of TIO's former insurance or banking business
GIVETH A `Can it be paid out of the Fund`
`s 17(2) -- can it be paid out of the Fund` `what` MEANS
    IF `a purpose listed in s 17(2)` `what`
    THEN `yes: that is one of the purposes for which the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund (s 17(2)); the Fund belongs to the Territory and is held by the Commission for it, not on trust (s 16(2), (3))`
    ELSE `no: the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund only for the purposes listed in s 17(2), and this is not one of them (the text's no)`

§§ `s 18 -- My treatment by NT Regional Health Services`

-- s 18(3): "MAC claimant means a person who is entitled to compensation under section 18 of the Motor Accidents
-- (Compensation) Act 1979" (borrowed: asked). "public health services means medical and rehabilitation services provided
-- by NT Regional Health Services that would have been compensable under section 18 of the Motor Accidents
-- (Compensation) Act 1979 had the services been provided by a person who is not part of NT Regional Health Services."
-- Both are "means" definitions: when a limb fails, the text's no. s 18(1): after each financial year "the Minister must
-- determine the amount (if any) that the Minister considers should be paid to reimburse the Territory for the cost of
-- providing public health services to MAC claimants"; s 18(2): the Commission must pay it out of the Fund within 2
-- months after the Minister notifies it (finding 3 on "the fee"). The Act does not say whether the claimant is charged.
GIVEN `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a MAC claimant` `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act` IF `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act`

GIVEN `medical or rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `by NT Regional Health Services` IS A BOOLEAN, `compensable if private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `public health services` `medical or rehabilitation` `by NT Regional Health Services` `compensable if private` IF
        `medical or rehabilitation`
    AND `by NT Regional Health Services`
    AND `compensable if private`

DECLARE `Is my public treatment reimbursed from the Fund` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are a MAC claimant and these are public health services, so their cost is among what the Minister must consider reimbursing to the Territory after the financial year, in the amount (if any) the Minister determines (s 18(1)); the Commission pays it out of the Fund within 2 months after the Minister's notice (s 18(2)); this Act does not say whether you are charged (NOTHING-kind)`
    `no: you are not a MAC claimant, a person entitled to compensation under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 18(3), the text's no)`
    `no: only medical and rehabilitation services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`
    `no: only services provided by NT Regional Health Services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no); a private provider's charges fall under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 itself`
    `no: the services would not have been compensable under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 had a private provider given them, so they are not public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`

@export I was treated by NT Regional Health Services (a public hospital or health service in the Northern Territory) after a motor accident. Is the cost of that treatment reimbursed to the Territory out of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Fund (s 18)?
GIVEN `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation for medical and rehabilitation expenses under section 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979
      `medical or rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services were medical or rehabilitation services
      `by NT Regional Health Services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services were provided by NT Regional Health Services (the Territory's public health service, section 10 of the Health Service Act 2021)
      `compensable if private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services would have been compensable under section 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 had a private provider given them
GIVETH A `Is my public treatment reimbursed from the Fund`
`s 18 -- is my public treatment reimbursed from the Fund` `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act` `medical or rehabilitation` `by NT Regional Health Services` `compensable if private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`a MAC claimant` `entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act`)) THEN `no: you are not a MAC claimant, a person entitled to compensation under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 18(3), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `medical or rehabilitation`) THEN `no: only medical and rehabilitation services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `by NT Regional Health Services`) THEN `no: only services provided by NT Regional Health Services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no); a private provider's charges fall under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 itself`
        IF (NOT `compensable if private`) THEN `no: the services would not have been compensable under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 had a private provider given them, so they are not public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are a MAC claimant and these are public health services, so their cost is among what the Minister must consider reimbursing to the Territory after the financial year, in the amount (if any) the Minister determines (s 18(1)); the Commission pays it out of the Fund within 2 months after the Minister's notice (s 18(2)); this Act does not say whether you are charged (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 28 -- Confidentiality of information about me`

-- s 28(1): "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person obtains information in the course of performing functions
-- connected with the administration of this Act; and (b) the person engages in conduct that results in the disclosure
-- of the information. Maximum penalty: 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years." s 28(2): strict liability applies
-- to (1)(a). s 28(3): (1) "does not apply if: (a) the person discloses the information: (i) for the administration of
-- this Act; or (ii) with the consent of the person to whom the information relates; or (iii) for legal proceedings
-- arising out of the operation of this Act; or (iv) for the proper performance of the Minister's ministerial functions
-- and duties; or (b) the information is otherwise available to the public." The note to s 28(3) points to s 43BE of the
-- Criminal Code (disclosure justified or excused by or under a law): borrowed, asked. Fork F5: information obtained in
-- administering the MAC scheme counts, since administering it is the Commission's function under s 7(a) of this Act.
DECLARE `Why it was disclosed` IS ONE OF
    `for the administration of this Act`
    `with my consent`
    `for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of this Act`
    `for the proper performance of the Minister's ministerial functions and duties`
    `for none of these`

GIVEN `why` IS A `Why it was disclosed`, `already public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excepted by s 28(3)` `why` `already public` IF
        `already public`
    OR  (CONSIDER `why`
         WHEN `for none of these` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule. The person who obtained the information shall not disclose it, unless the
-- disclosure is excepted by s 28(3): an excepted disclosure does not match the action (EXACTLY FALSE). The Act sets no
-- period; the rule's window of 1 is only the span of the trace in which the one disclosure asked about happens (on day
-- 0), so that the trace can end (finding 6).
DECLARE `Holder of the information` IS ONE OF `the person who obtained the information`
DECLARE `Disclosure step` IS ONE OF
    `engage in conduct that results in disclosing the information` HAS `excepted by s 28(3)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Holder of the information` `Disclosure step`
`s 28 -- do not disclose the information` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who obtained the information`
    SHANT `engage in conduct that results in disclosing the information` (EXACTLY FALSE)
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person who obtained the information` BECAUSE "the information was disclosed, and none of the exceptions in s 28(3) applies (s 28(1))"

-- Runs the rule over what happened. A CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH on the stable l4, so
-- FULFILLED means the prohibition was kept and anything else a breach. Not exported; takes no DEONTIC from outside.
GIVEN `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN, `excepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` `disclosed` `excepted` IF
    IF `disclosed`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 28 -- do not disclose the information` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person who obtained the information` (`engage in conduct that results in disclosing the information` `excepted`) 0), (WAITUNTIL 2))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 28 -- do not disclose the information` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 2))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Was disclosing my information an offence` IS ONE OF
    `no: s 28 does not reach it, since the person did not obtain the information in performing functions connected with the administration of this Act (s 28(1)(a), the text's no)`
    `no: nothing was disclosed (s 28(1)(b), the text's no)`
    `no: s 28(1) does not apply to a disclosure for the administration of this Act, with your consent, for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of this Act, or for the Minister's proper ministerial functions, or of information otherwise available to the public (s 28(3), the text's no)`
    `the elements of s 28(1) are met, but the person is not criminally responsible if the disclosure was justified or excused by or under a law (Criminal Code s 43BE, as the note to s 28(3) says); as you state it, it was`
    `yes: the elements of the offence in s 28(1) are met (strict liability applies to how the information was obtained, s 28(2)); maximum penalty 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years; whether there is a conviction is for a court`

@export Was it an offence under s 28 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT) for someone working on the scheme to disclose information about me?
GIVEN `obtained in administering the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person obtained the information in the course of performing functions connected with the administration of the Act, for example working for the Commission or its claims agent on the MAC scheme or the Fund
      `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person did something that resulted in the information being disclosed
      `why` IS A `Why it was disclosed` @desc Why it was disclosed: for the administration of the Act; with your consent (you are the person the information is about); for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of the Act; for the proper performance of the Minister's ministerial functions and duties; or for none of these
      `already public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information was otherwise available to the public
      `justified by another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure was justified or excused by or under another law (Criminal Code s 43BE; a court decides this)
GIVETH A `Was disclosing my information an offence`
`s 28 -- was disclosing my information an offence` `obtained in administering the Act` `disclosed` `why` `already public` `justified by another law` MEANS
    IF (NOT `obtained in administering the Act`)
    THEN `no: s 28 does not reach it, since the person did not obtain the information in performing functions connected with the administration of this Act (s 28(1)(a), the text's no)`
    ELSE IF `s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` `disclosed` (`excepted by s 28(3)` `why` `already public`)
         THEN IF `disclosed`
              THEN `no: s 28(1) does not apply to a disclosure for the administration of this Act, with your consent, for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of this Act, or for the Minister's proper ministerial functions, or of information otherwise available to the public (s 28(3), the text's no)`
              ELSE `no: nothing was disclosed (s 28(1)(b), the text's no)`
         ELSE IF `justified by another law`
              THEN `the elements of s 28(1) are met, but the person is not criminally responsible if the disclosure was justified or excused by or under a law (Criminal Code s 43BE, as the note to s 28(3) says); as you state it, it was`
              ELSE `yes: the elements of the offence in s 28(1) are met (strict liability applies to how the information was obtained, s 28(2)); maximum penalty 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years; whether there is a conviction is for a court`

-- s 28(1): "Maximum penalty: 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years." The value of a penalty unit is set under
-- the Penalty Units Act 2009 (NT), not deposited: asked.
`s 28 -- penalty units` MEANS 200

@export What is the most a person can be fined for disclosing information about me in breach of s 28 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT)? The maximum is 200 penalty units (or imprisonment for 2 years instead); the answer is in dollars.
GIVEN `value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one Northern Territory penalty unit in dollars on the day of the offence, as set under the Penalty Units Act 2009 (NT)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 28 -- the most I could see them fined` `value of a penalty unit` MEANS `s 28 -- penalty units` TIMES `value of a penalty unit`

§§ `s 12(3) -- A document under the Commission's seal`

-- s 12(3): "A document purporting to bear the common seal of the Commission is taken to have been duly executed by the
-- Commission, in the absence of evidence to the contrary." Without the seal, s 12(3) says nothing (NOTHING-kind); with
-- evidence to the contrary, the presumption gives way and the Act does not say whether it was executed (fork F7).
DECLARE `Is the sealed document taken as the Commission's` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a document that purports to bear the Commission's common seal is taken to have been duly executed by the Commission (s 12(3))`
    `this Act does not say: the presumption in s 12(3) gives way to evidence to the contrary, and whether the Commission executed it is then a question of fact (NOTHING-kind)`
    `this Act does not say: s 12(3) speaks only of documents bearing the Commission's common seal (NOTHING-kind)`

@export A document I received from the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission bears its common seal. Is it taken to have been properly executed by the Commission (s 12(3))?
GIVEN `bears the seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document bears, or appears to bear, the Commission's common seal
      `evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence that the Commission did not in fact duly execute it
GIVETH A `Is the sealed document taken as the Commission's`
`s 12(3) -- is the sealed document taken as the Commission's` `bears the seal` `evidence to the contrary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `bears the seal`) THEN `this Act does not say: s 12(3) speaks only of documents bearing the Commission's common seal (NOTHING-kind)`
        IF `evidence to the contrary` THEN `this Act does not say: the presumption in s 12(3) gives way to evidence to the contrary, and whether the Commission executed it is then a question of fact (NOTHING-kind)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: a document that purports to bear the Commission's common seal is taken to have been duly executed by the Commission (s 12(3))`

§§ `s 5(1), s 43 -- A claim or step taken with TIO before 2015 (only if you dealt with the Territory Insurance Office)`

-- s 5(1): TIO "continues as the same corporate entity" as the Commission. s 43(1): "Anything done or omitted to be done
-- by, to, or in relation to, TIO before the commencement of this Act that is of ongoing effect is to be taken, after that
-- commencement, to have been done or omitted to be done by, to, or in relation to, the Commission." s 43(2): if done for
-- a provision of the TIO Act, it is taken to have been done for the equivalent provision of this Act. The commencement
-- is a period the text fixes: after it, the text's no. "That is of ongoing effect" is a scope limit with no "only":
-- NOTHING-kind (fork F8). Whether a step is of ongoing effect is asked.
DECLARE `Does what was done with TIO still count` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is taken to have been done by, to or in relation to the Commission (s 43(1)), which is TIO continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1)); if it was done for a provision of the Territory Insurance Office Act 1979, it counts for the equivalent provision of this Act (s 43(2))`
    `s 43 does not carry it over, since it was not of ongoing effect (NOTHING-kind); the Commission is still the same corporate entity as TIO (s 5(1))`
    `no: s 43 covers only what was done before the Act commenced on 1 January 2015 (the text's no); by then TIO was already the Commission, continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1))`

@export I lodged a claim, gave a notice or took another step with the Territory Insurance Office (TIO) before 2015, or TIO did something about my matter. Does it still count now that TIO is the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission (s 5(1), s 43)?
GIVEN `done on` IS A DATE @desc The day the step was taken (or the thing done or not done)
      `ongoing effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the step still had effect when the Act commenced on 1 January 2015, for example a claim not yet finally dealt with
GIVETH A `Does what was done with TIO still count`
`s 5(1), s 43 -- does what was done with TIO still count` `done on` `ongoing effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`before the commencement of the Act` `done on`)) THEN `no: s 43 covers only what was done before the Act commenced on 1 January 2015 (the text's no); by then TIO was already the Commission, continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1))`
        IF `ongoing effect` THEN `yes: it is taken to have been done by, to or in relation to the Commission (s 43(1)), which is TIO continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1)); if it was done for a provision of the Territory Insurance Office Act 1979, it counts for the equivalent provision of this Act (s 43(2))`
        OTHERWISE `s 43 does not carry it over, since it was not of ongoing effect (NOTHING-kind); the Commission is still the same corporate entity as TIO (s 5(1))`

§§ `s 30, ss 31, 33, 34 -- My old TIO policy or deposit (only if you were a TIO customer)`

-- s 30(1): "The Commission has the function of winding up the residual insurance business": so much of TIO's insurance
-- business as was not included in the sale (s 30(3)). s 33(2): the Commission carries on "the residual banking business
-- until all residual deposits have been repaid" and winds it up; residual deposit means "a deposit held by the
-- Commission as part of the residual banking business" (s 31). s 34(1): those moneys are the Territory's, held by the
-- Commission; s 34(2): used for no other purpose. What was included in the sale is governed by the Territory Insurance
-- Office (Sale) Act 2014, not deposited: NOTHING-kind here.
DECLARE `My old TIO matter` IS ONE OF
    `an insurance policy or claim with TIO`
    `a deposit with TIO`

DECLARE `Who deals with my old TIO matter` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission: it has the function of winding up TIO's residual insurance business, the part not included in the sale (s 30(1), (3)); s 27's guarantee does not cover it (NOTHING-kind)`
    `the Commission: it carries on TIO's residual banking business until all residual deposits have been repaid, and then winds it up (s 33(2)); the moneys of that business are the Territory's property, held by the Commission and used for no other purpose (s 34(1), (2))`
    `not this Act: your policy or deposit went with the sale under the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014, and this Act does not say who deals with it (NOTHING-kind)`

@export I had an insurance policy, a claim or a deposit with the Territory Insurance Office (TIO). Who deals with it now (s 30, s 33, s 34)?
GIVEN `matter` IS A `My old TIO matter` @desc What you had with TIO: an insurance policy or claim, or a deposit
      `included in the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your policy or deposit was included in the sale of TIO's insurance or banking business under the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014
GIVETH A `Who deals with my old TIO matter`
`s 30, s 33 -- who deals with my old TIO matter` `matter` `included in the sale` MEANS
    IF `included in the sale`
    THEN `not this Act: your policy or deposit went with the sale under the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014, and this Act does not say who deals with it (NOTHING-kind)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `matter`
         WHEN `an insurance policy or claim with TIO` THEN `the Commission: it has the function of winding up TIO's residual insurance business, the part not included in the sale (s 30(1), (3)); s 27's guarantee does not cover it (NOTHING-kind)`
         WHEN `a deposit with TIO` THEN `the Commission: it carries on TIO's residual banking business until all residual deposits have been repaid, and then winds it up (s 33(2)); the moneys of that business are the Territory's property, held by the Commission and used for no other purpose (s 34(1), (2))`
